In the absence of a byfy or equivalent/replacement, there is no entity=20
other than the Board (or members during a meeting) that can or should=20
approve ANY change to the language.  That was the state before byfy, and=20
again is the state until it is replaced.

But if course, if I am correct that it wasn't properly discussed, then=20
it can and should wait for an organization to be properly constituted (I=20
won't pretend to understand the convoluted mess that passed during the=20
meeting, but I had the impression that said approved proposal would in=20
face require formally documented proposals before they are decided).

Certainly this proposal is NOT merely the correction of an error in the=20
original CLL, and if not formally approved.  My understanding is that=20
the update to CLL is not supposed to be changing anything that wasn't=20
part of the original language (and erroneously described) or some=20
language change proposal that was approved by byfy before it was=20
disconstituted.

Remember that I personally don't support language changes *in general*=20
unless they are fixing something broken, though I can only control my=20
own vote, such as it is.

